# The de Havilland Mosquito FB Mk VI's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/mosquito-fb6.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The Mosquito has no airbrake and no spoiler, so nothing here names one. Its
# radiator shutters are open or shut and nothing between, and its supercharger
# switch is AUTO or MOD, so both are read as over or under half.
#
# The Notes give no approach speed that has been found. The figures here are
# worked from their stalling speeds in assets/figures/mosquito-fb6.xml -
# 95 to 100 knots with the undercarriage and flaps down - a third above the
# stall on the approach and a sixth over the boundary. The rest are the Notes'
# own: 3,000 rpm for take-off, 2,850 for the climb, 2,650 continuous.

phase before-start
confirm Chocks in, the fire guard posted and the propellers called clear
confirm Fuel cocks on the main tanks, and the contents checked
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture levers up, where the carburettors do the rest
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.2 Throttles half an inch open
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Propeller levers fully forward, fully fine
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open for the ground

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 600 Port engine running and warming
check propulsion/engine[1]/engine-rpm >= 600 Starboard engine running and warming
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open: a Merlin boils on the ground
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
confirm Brakes checked as the aircraft first moves, and the tail wheel free to castor
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi on low power, turning on the outer throttle

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 15.5 Flaps up, or fifteen degrees for a short run
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Propeller levers fully fine, for 3,000 rpm
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Elevator trim set for take-off
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttles opened slowly to full, the swing held on the rudder
check velocities/vc-kts >= 100 Unstick at about 100 knots and hold her down to the safety speed

phase climb
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up once there is no runway left to land on
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up by the safety speed, 155 knots at climbing power
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2600 2950 Propeller levers back to the climbing gate, 2,850 rpm
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open for the climb
range velocities/vc-kts 130 170 Climb at 148 knots, the Notes' 170 mph
check fcs/supercharger-cmd-norm >= 0.5 Supercharger switch at AUTO: FS gear comes in through 7,000 feet

phase cruise
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] <= 0.5 Radiator shutters shut: open they cost the aircraft its speed
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2000 2700 Propellers at 2,650 rpm or below, the continuous limit
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check gear/gear-pos-norm <= 0.05 Undercarriage up
confirm Drop tanks used first, and the cocks changed before either main tank runs low

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.1 0.6 Throttles back, but kept open enough to keep the engines warm
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] <= 0.5 Radiator shutters shut while the engines are cooling anyway
check fcs/supercharger-cmd-norm >= 0.5 Supercharger at AUTO: MS gear returns below 6,500 feet
confirm Altimeter set to the aerodrome's pressure
confirm Fuel cocks back on the main tanks before the circuit

phase approach
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked, and the indicators seen
check fcs/advance-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Propeller levers fully fine, for the power a go-around would need
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 20.0 45.5 Flaps down for the approach
range velocities/vc-kts 115 140 Approach at 125 knots, a third above the stall with everything down
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open again for the slow running

phase landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg >= 40.0 Flaps fully down, forty-five degrees
check gear/gear-pos-norm >= 0.95 Undercarriage down and locked
range velocities/vc-kts 105 120 Over the boundary at 110 knots
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.2 Throttles closed in the hold-off
confirm Wheels first with the tail up, and the brakes only once the speed has gone

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/cooling-flaps-cmd-norm[0] >= 0.5 Radiator shutters open for the taxi in
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttles back to a taxi power
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
confirm Brakes tried again, and the ground crew waved in ahead of the wing tips
